# Dropbear's default 24 KB channel receive window stalls downloads on this
# board: the Wi-Fi link idles in power save, so small packets see a ~90 ms
# effective RTT (DTIM/beacon wakeup).  A 24 KB window with window adjustments
# every 8 KB caps a single channel at roughly 260 KB/s regardless of the
# 24 Mbps the radio can actually sustain.  A 1 MB window measured 5x faster
# (2 -> 10 Mbps); larger windows gave nothing more, since the remaining limit
# is the 408 MHz CPU doing chacha20.
DROPBEAR_ARGS="-W 262144"
